# The origin of the Next app this client talks to.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and set the value for your machine. It is not
# committed with a default on purpose: in local development this is the devcontainer's published
# app port, and that port is derived from a hash of the worktree path — so it differs per worktree
# and per machine. A committed default would be right for exactly one checkout and quietly wrong
# for every other one.
#
# Find yours from the repository root:
#
#   grep PORT .devcontainer/docker-compose.worktree.yml
#
# The iOS Simulator shares the host's network stack, so `localhost` reaches the Mac, and the
# container publishes the app there. A *physical* device does not — it needs the Mac's LAN IP
# instead, and the web server's own `resolveBaseUrl()` has to agree, which means setting `APP_URL`
# to that same address in the repository root's `.env.local`.
#
# Production is not configured here. A release build takes its value from the EAS build profile,
# so a shipped binary can never accidentally carry a developer's localhost.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:55080
